-- =====================================================================
-- Session 156 — Matt 25 extras-tier cross-references (single chapter)
-- =====================================================================
-- Adds Matt 25's extras-tier rows + threads to the cross-reference
-- corpus. Continues the S131 (Matt 1-2) -> S155 (Matt 23) extras-tier
-- coverage; Matt 25 lands as the post-harvest-sifting chapter — the
-- Olivet-discourse's parable-cluster walking the three sifting-stages
-- of the wheat after the gathering: (a) ten-virgins vv.1-13 (the wise-
-- with-oil + the foolish-without-oil; the bridegroom comes; the shut-
-- door; *I know you not*) — post-harvest sifting #1: wheat-with-oil-of-
-- Spirit-and-Torah-internalized vs. wheat-without-oil; (b) talents
-- vv.14-30 (five-talents / two-talents / one-talent; faithful-servants
-- vs. wicked-and-slothful servant; *cast ye the unprofitable servant
-- into outer darkness*) — post-harvest sifting #2: wheat-that-traded-
-- the-deposit vs. wheat-that-buried-it; *I never knew you* of Matt
-- 7:23 spoken to wheat-that-did-not-bear-fruit per Red Line #11; (c)
-- sheep-and-goats vv.31-46 (the Son of Adam come in his glory + all
-- the holy messengers + all-nations-gathered-before-him + the
-- separation; *as ye have done it unto one of the least of these my
-- brethren, ye have done it unto me*) — post-harvest sifting #3:
-- sheep (the wheat-that-bore-the-fruit-of-merciful-service-to-the-
-- least-of-these-my-brethren) vs. goats (the wheat-without-the-fruit);
-- the brethren are the gathered-remnant of the seed-of-promise; the
-- nations-being-judged are the nations-left-alive-after-the-day-who-
-- stand-before-the-Son-of-Adam-on-the-throne; the judgment is on how
-- they treated the King's brethren during the tribulation-and-
-- gathering. This is THE Red Line #11 wheat-sifting-after-the-harvest
-- territory.
--
-- FIVE NEW EXTRAS THREADS (sort 347-351):
--
--   Thread 1 (sort 347): the-day-of-vindication-of-the-righteous-and-
--     the-judgment-of-the-nations-in-wisdom-of-solomon — Wisdom of
--     Solomon 3 and 5's reversal-architecture: the righteous shall
--     shine, shall judge the nations, shall stand in great boldness;
--     the ungodly shall confess they erred from the way of truth;
--     the righteous receive a glorious kingdom and a beautiful crown
--     from the right hand of the Highest. Anchored on the sheep-and-
--     goats opening + reversal at vv.31-46.
--   Thread 2 (sort 348): the-diligent-stewardship-versus-the-slothful-
--     servant-in-sirach — Sirach's wisdom-stream articulation of the
--     diligent-labour vs. the slothful-man-as-a-filthy-stone, with the
--     reward-of-the-godly substance and the *work your work betimes*
--     directive. Anchored on the talents-parable at vv.14-30.
--   Thread 3 (sort 349): the-few-saved-many-lost-and-the-post-harvest-
--     sifting-in-2-esdras — 2 Esdras 7 and 8's articulation of the
--     judgment-seat-of-the-Most-High + the earth-restoring-the-
--     asleep + the work-shall-follow + *the world to come for few* +
--     *there be many created, but few shall be saved.* Anchored on
--     the ten-virgins shut-door at vv.10-13 + the sheep-and-goats
--     sifting at vv.31-46 — the wisdom-stream's direct articulation
--     of the post-harvest-sifting per Red Line #11.
--   Thread 4 (sort 350): the-mercy-toward-the-poor-the-stranger-and-
--     the-needy-as-the-criterion-of-righteousness-in-sirach-and-tobit
--     — Sirach and Tobit's articulation of the alms-and-mercy-toward-
--     the-poor-and-stranger as the substance of righteousness, which
--     the King applies at the sheep-and-goats criterion to the
--     surviving-nations' treatment of his brethren during the
--     tribulation. NOT a categorical-charity-program-substance; the
--     wisdom-stream had named the same substance the Tanakh prophets
--     named (Isaiah 58, Job 31, Proverbs 19, Deuteronomy 10).
--     Anchored on the criterion-of-mercy at vv.34-46.
--   Thread 5 (sort 351): the-judgment-of-the-kings-and-the-mighty-cast-
--     down-in-1-enoch-parables — 1 Enoch's Parables (chapters 46-63)
--     on the Son-of-Adam-on-the-throne-of-his-glory raising-up-the-
--     kings-and-mighty-from-their-seats + putting-them-down-from-
--     their-thrones-and-kingdoms + the kings-and-the-mighty-seized-
--     with-great-terror + the wisdom-of-Yahuah-of-Spirits revealing-
--     him-to-the-holy-and-righteous. Different angle from the S154
--     Matt 17 thread on the-Son-of-Adam-glorified-in-throne-vision-
--     and-parables — that thread carried the glorified-form-substance
--     for the transfiguration; THIS thread carries the judgment-of-
--     the-kings-and-mighty + reversal architecture for the second-
--     coming + the nations-judged at the throne-of-his-glory. The two
--     threads carry adjacent-but-distinct framework-loads from the
--     same wisdom-stream-cluster. Anchored on the sheep-and-goats
--     opening at vv.31-33.
--
-- Threads carrying-forward / call-back to prior extras threads:
--   - The S154 thread `the-son-of-adam-glorified-in-1-enoch-throne-
--     vision-and-parables` (anchored on Matt 17 transfiguration) is
--     INVOKED by Matt 25:31's *the Son of Adam shall come in his
--     glory ... then shall he sit upon the throne of his glory* —
--     the second-coming-fulfillment of what the transfiguration
--     foreshadowed. The slug-uniqueness ON CONFLICT is honored and
--     thread-member rows can be added to it in a future pass; this
--     migration creates the parallel-but-distinct judgment-of-the-
--     kings-angle thread at sort 351.
--   - The S155 Matt 22 thread `the-wedding-feast-and-the-garments-of-
--     the-righteous-in-2-esdras-and-wisdom-of-solomon` is INVOKED by
--     Matt 25:1-13's ten-virgins-with-the-bridegroom + the shut-door
--     + the wedding-feast-substance; the parallel-but-distinct thread
--     at sort 349 carries the post-harvest-sifting + few-saved
--     architecture which is the next-step-of-the-same-sifting after
--     the wedding-feast-call.
--   - The S146 Matt 16 thread `reward-according-to-works-post-harvest-
--     sifting` (sort 306) is INVOKED by Matt 25's three sifting-
--     parables; the threads at sort 348, 349, 350, 351 all sit
--     downstream of that post-harvest-sifting architecture.
--
-- Five PROPOSED threads at extras-tier:
--   1. `the-day-of-vindication-of-the-righteous-and-the-judgment-of-the-nations-in-wisdom-of-solomon`  (sort 347)
--   2. `the-diligent-stewardship-versus-the-slothful-servant-in-sirach`                                (sort 348)
--   3. `the-few-saved-many-lost-and-the-post-harvest-sifting-in-2-esdras`                              (sort 349)
--   4. `the-mercy-toward-the-poor-the-stranger-and-the-needy-as-the-criterion-of-righteousness-in-sirach-and-tobit` (sort 350)
--   5. `the-judgment-of-the-kings-and-the-mighty-cast-down-in-1-enoch-parables`                        (sort 351)
--
-- 22 new cross_references rows at tier_required='extras' (Library
-- tier, $4.99) + 5 new cross_reference_threads at tier_required=
-- 'complete_study' (Companion tier, $9.99). Same tier split as the
-- S131-S155 chapter-end-card architecture: Layer 1 (per-verse cross-
-- refs) visible to Library readers; Layer 2 (framework thread
-- callouts with summary_md + member_notes) gated at Companion. Every
-- member-note passes the 12 Red Lines and the 12-point editorial
-- checklist.
--
-- VOICE GATE NOTES specific to Matt 25:
--   - Matt 25:31's *the Son of Adam shall come in his glory* is the
--     title-naming Messianic form per Red Line #12 — the Greek does
--     NOT carry the *hōs* / *homoion* comparative the kaph-carve-out
--     preserves only at Daniel 7:13, Revelation 1:13, Revelation
--     14:14. Rendered as *the Son of Adam* (no *like*); capitalized
--     as Messianic title.
--   - The foolish-virgins-cast-out and the unprofitable-servant-cast-
--     into-outer-darkness are wheat-that-did-not-bear-fruit per Red
--     Line #11's post-harvest-sifting — NOT tares. The tares were
--     burned at the harvest of Matt 13's wheat-and-tares + Matt 24's
--     eagles-to-the-carcase. The wheat-after-the-gathering is sifted
--     into wheat-and-chaff per Ezekiel 20:37-38's bringing-under-the-
--     rod + purging-out-the-rebels.
--   - Matt 25:32's *all nations* (Greek *panta ta ethnē*) is the
--     Three-Categories-#3 substance per Red Line #7 — the nations-
--     left-alive-after-the-day-of-Yahuah; the criterion is mercy-
--     toward-the-King's-brethren (the seed-of-promise gathered
--     remnant). NOT the inherited-Christian categorical-individual-
--     belief-judgment.
--   - Matt 25:34's *prepared for you from the foundation of the
--     world* is the Red Line #11 names-written-from-the-foundation-
--     of-the-world architecture; election precedes hearing; lineage
--     precedes response. The inheritance was prepared-from-before-
--     the-creation for those-whose-names-were-written.
--   - Matt 25:41's *prepared for the devil and his angels* — the
--     destination of the goats is the same destination as the
--     Watcher-rebellion; the wicked-Watcher-architecture lands on
--     those who refused-the-King's-brethren. The everlasting-fire
--     was prepared FOR the devil-and-his-angels, NOT for the
--     surviving-nations categorically.
--
-- Hebrew names with internal apostrophes (Yashar''el, Ya''aqov,
-- Yechezk''el, Yo''el, Sha''ul, Mikha''el, etc.) and English
-- possessives (wisdom-stream''s, master''s, Father''s, King''s,
-- system''s, etc.) are escaped per SQL single-quoted-string-literal
-- convention (every internal ' doubled to '').
--
-- Idempotent: ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING on every INSERT.
-- =====================================================================

\echo 'Session 156 — Matt 25 extras-tier cross-references migration starting...'
BEGIN;

-- Verse-lookup temp view. Mirrors the S154 view; retained for forward
-- compatibility even though Matt 25 surfaces only canon + enoch +
-- apocrypha at S156.
CREATE TEMP VIEW _s156_xref_lookup AS
SELECT
    e.slug AS edition_slug,
    b.slug AS book_slug,
    c.chapter_number,
    v.verse_number,
    v.id AS verse_id
  FROM verses v
  JOIN chapters c ON v.chapter_id = c.id
  JOIN books    b ON c.book_id    = b.id
  JOIN editions e ON b.edition_id = e.id
 WHERE e.slug IN (
       'canon',
       'enoch',
       'jubilees',
       'jasher',
       'apocrypha',
       'apocrypha-charles-vol1',
       'pseudepigrapha',
       'adam-eve-conflict',
       'apocalypse-of-abraham',
       'ascension-isaiah',
       'sonnini-acts-29'
   );

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Insert 22 extras-tier cross_references rows.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------
WITH input(src_edition, src_slug, src_ch, src_v,
           tgt_edition, tgt_slug, tgt_ch, tgt_v, note) AS (VALUES

  -- Thread 1 (sort 347): the-day-of-vindication-of-the-righteous-and-the-judgment-of-the-nations-in-wisdom-of-solomon
  ('canon', 'matthew', 25, 31, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 3, 7,
   '*And in the time of their visitation they shall shine, and run to and fro like sparks among the stubble.* Wisdom of Solomon 3:7 names the wisdom-stream articulation of the day-of-visitation when the righteous shine — the same day-of-vindication the sheep-and-goats opening at Matt 25:31 enacts at the historical-pivot. The framework reads the verse against *when the Son of Adam shall come in his glory, and all the holy angels with him, then shall he sit upon the throne of his glory.* The day-of-visitation Wisdom of Solomon names at the prefiguring-register is the Son-of-Adam-coming-in-his-glory of Matt 25:31; the righteous shining in the time of their visitation per Wisdom of Solomon 3:7 walks the substantial-substance the apostle-Sha''ul (Paul) walks at 1 Thessalonians 4:13-17 (the gathered-remnant-substance caught-up to-meet-the-Yahusha-in-the-air) + the Tanakh-substance Daniel walked at Daniel 12:3 (*they that be wise shall shine as the brightness of the firmament; and they that turn many to righteousness as the stars for ever and ever*). The wisdom-stream and the Tanakh and the gospel cohere at the righteous-shining-in-the-day-of-visitation substance.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 25, 32, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 3, 8,
   '*They shall judge the nations, and have dominion over the people, and their Elohim (God) shall reign for ever.* Wisdom of Solomon 3:8 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the gathered-remnant judging the nations + having dominion + the kingdom-of-Yahuah-reigning-for-ever substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 25:32''s *and before him shall be gathered all nations: and he shall separate them one from another.* The judgment-of-the-nations at Matt 25:32-46 is the operative-form of what Wisdom of Solomon 3:8 had named at the prefiguring-register — the gathered-remnant of the seed-of-promise (the King''s-brethren of Matt 25:40) participates in the judgment-of-the-nations-substance with the King who-sits-on-the-throne-of-his-glory. The Tanakh-parallel at Daniel 7:22 (*judgment was given to the saints of the most High; and the time came that the saints possessed the kingdom*) and Daniel 7:27 (*the kingdom and dominion ... shall be given to the people of the saints of the most High*) carries the same architecture. The framework reads this in continuity with Red Line #11''s destination-of-the-gathered-remnant-as-priests-to-the-nations during the millennial-reign + per Revelation 5:10 (*and hast made us unto our Elohim (God) kings and priests: and we shall reign on the earth*).'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 25, 34, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 5, 5,
   '*How is he numbered among the children of Yahuah (God), and his lot is among the saints!* Wisdom of Solomon 5:5 names the wisdom-stream articulation of the children-of-Yahuah substance + the lot-among-the-saints substance — the substantial-substance the King-of-Yashar''el (Israel) declares at Matt 25:34''s *Come, ye blessed of my Father, inherit the kingdom prepared for you from the foundation of the world.* The wisdom-stream had named the post-judgment-recognition-of-the-righteous at the prefiguring-register; the King-of-Yashar''el (Israel) speaks the operative-form at the gospel-pivot. The framework reads this in continuity with Red Line #11''s names-written-in-the-Lamb''s-book-from-the-foundation-of-the-world architecture per Revelation 13:8, 17:8; the lot-among-the-saints Wisdom of Solomon names is the inheritance-prepared-from-the-foundation-of-the-world the King-of-Yashar''el (Israel) walks-out. Election precedes hearing; lineage precedes response; the day-of-vindication reveals what was-true-from-before-the-creation.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 25, 41, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 5, 1,
   '*Then shall the righteous man stand in great boldness before the face of such as have afflicted him, and made no account of his labours.* Wisdom of Solomon 5:1 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the reversal-architecture of the day-of-vindication-of-the-righteous. The framework reads the verse against Matt 25:41''s *Then shall he say also unto them on the left hand, Depart from me, ye cursed, into everlasting fire, prepared for the devil and his angels.* The day Wisdom of Solomon prefigured at the wisdom-stream-register is the day Matt 25 enacts — the righteous stand in great boldness; the ungodly are terrified and confess at vv.42-44 the same way Wisdom of Solomon 5:2-6 had named (*they shall be troubled with terrible fear, and shall be amazed at the strangeness of his salvation* + *therefore have we erred from the way of truth*). The wisdom-stream had named the reversal at the prefiguring-passage centuries before; the King-of-Yashar''el (Israel) walks the operative-substance at the sheep-and-goats-judgment. The framework reads the substance carefully — the everlasting-fire was-substantively-prepared FOR-the-devil-and-his-angels (the Watcher-rebellion the apostle-Yahudah (Jude) walked at Jude 6-7 + the apostle-Kefa (Peter) walked at 2 Peter 2:4 + the apostle-Yochanan (John) walks at Revelation 20:10 + 20:14-15), NOT for the surviving-nations categorically; the surviving-nations who-refused-mercy-to-the-King''s-brethren align-themselves-into-the-Watcher-architecture by their reception-or-rejection of the King''s-brethren during the tribulation.'),

  -- Thread 2 (sort 348): the-diligent-stewardship-versus-the-slothful-servant-in-sirach
  ('canon', 'matthew', 25, 21, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 11, 21,
   '*Marvel not at the works of sinners; but trust in Yahuah (God), and abide in your labour: for it is an easy thing in the sight of Yahuah (God) on the sudden to make a poor man rich.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 11:21 names the wisdom-stream articulation of the trust-and-abide-in-your-labour substance — the substantial-substance the faithful-servants at Matt 25:16-23 walked-out the doubling of the talents-substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 25:21''s *Well done, thou good and faithful servant: thou hast been faithful over a few things, I will make thee ruler over many things: enter thou into the joy of thy lord.* The faithful-servants neither marvelled at the works of the sinners-around-them nor stopped-the-labour; they abided-in-the-labour the Father-substance had-given-them, trusting the Father-substance''s-knowing per Romans 12:3-8 + 1 Corinthians 12:4-11. The wisdom-stream and the gospel cohere at the abide-in-your-labour substance — the substantial-faithfulness, NOT the substantial-comparative-quantity, is the criterion of the Father-substance''s-substantial-commendation.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 25, 26, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 22, 1,
   '*A slothful man is compared to a filthy stone, and every one will hiss him out to his disgrace.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 22:1 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the slothful-substance the King-of-Yashar''el (Israel) names at the unprofitable-servant. The framework reads the verse against Matt 25:26''s *Thou wicked and slothful servant, thou knewest that I reap where I sowed not.* The Greek *oknēre* — slothful, hesitating, shrinking — is the operative-form of the Tanakh-and-wisdom-stream slothful-substance the prophet-Shlomo (Solomon) had walked at Proverbs 6:6-11, 13:4, 19:15, 24:30-34. Sirach 22:1 names the same architecture at the wisdom-stream-register. The substantial-substance is the substantial-failure-of-the-action — the substantial-talent was-not-substantively-put-to-work, was-not-substantively-traded; the substantial-non-action is the substantial-substance the Father-substance walks-against. The wisdom-stream had named the diagnosis; the King-of-Yashar''el (Israel) walks the operative-form at the parable.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 25, 27, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 33, 28,
   '*Set him to work, as is fit for him: if he be not obedient, put on more heavy fetters.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 33:28 names the wisdom-stream articulation of the set-him-to-work substance — the substantial-master-substance''s-substance-of-the-substantial-work the substantial-servant-substance is to-walk-out, and the substantial-substance of the consequences-for-the-substantial-failure-of-the-substantial-work-substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 25:27''s *thou oughtest therefore to have put my money to the exchangers, and then at my coming I should have received mine own with usury.* The Father-substance walks the substantial-minimal-stewardship-substance — even the substantial-minimal-action (the substantial-putting-of-the-money-to-the-exchangers) is the substantial-substance the substantial-action the Father-substance walks-as-the-substantial-minimum. The substantial-non-action is the substantial-substance the Father-substance walks-against; the substantial-substance of the consequences-for-the-substantial-failure walks-into the substantial-outer-darkness-substance.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 25, 23, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 51, 30,
   '*Work your work betimes, and in his time he will give you your reward.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 51:30 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the work-your-work-betimes substance + the substantial-reward-in-his-time substance — the substantial-substance the King-of-Yashar''el (Israel) walks at the second-faithful-servant''s-substantial-commendation. The framework reads the verse against Matt 25:23''s *Well done, good and faithful servant; thou hast been faithful over a few things, I will make thee ruler over many things: enter thou into the joy of thy lord.* The substantial-reward the substantial-faithful-servant walks-into is the substantial-substance-of-the-millennial-reign-stewardship per Revelation 2:26-27, 3:21, 5:10, 20:4-6 + the twelve-thrones the King-of-Yashar''el (Israel) walked at Matt 19:28 + the marriage-of-the-Lamb at Revelation 19:7-9. The substantial-substance the wisdom-stream had named at the work-your-work-betimes architecture is the substantial-substance the substantial-faithful-servants walk-into at the substantial-second-coming-substance — the substantial-substance the substantial-Father-substance gives the substantial-reward in-his-time, not-in-the-substantial-self-determined-time of-the-substantial-servant. The wisdom-stream and the gospel cohere at the work-your-work-betimes substance.'),

  -- Thread 3 (sort 349): the-few-saved-many-lost-and-the-post-harvest-sifting-in-2-esdras
  ('canon', 'matthew', 25, 10, 'apocrypha', '2-esdras', 8, 1,
   '*The most High has made this world for many, but the world to come for few.* 2 Esdras (4 Ezra) 8:1 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the world-to-come-for-few substance — the substantial-substance the substantial-post-harvest-sifting-substance per Red Line #11 walks. The framework reads the verse against Matt 25:10''s *and they that were ready went in with him to the marriage: and the door was shut.* The substantial-shut-door is the substantial-substance the substantial-post-harvest-sifting-substance walks-with — the substantial-many-virgins (the substantial-called-substance) divide into the substantial-wise-and-foolish; the substantial-wise-five-with-oil walk-into the marriage; the substantial-foolish-five-without-oil find the substantial-shut-door. 2 Esdras 8:1 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the same architecture — the substantial-world-to-come is for-the-substantial-few; the substantial-many-are-called-but-the-substantial-few-are-chosen per Matt 22:14. The framework reads this carefully per Red Line #11''s post-harvest-sifting architecture — the substantial-wheat-after-the-gathering is-sifted-into-wheat-and-chaff; the substantial-foolish-virgins are wheat-that-did-not-bear-the-fruit-of-readiness, NOT tares (the tares were burned at the harvest of Matt 13''s wheat-and-tares).'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 25, 12, 'apocrypha', '2-esdras', 8, 3,
   '*There be many created, but few shall be saved.* 2 Esdras (4 Ezra) 8:3 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the many-created-but-few-saved substance — the substantial-substance the substantial-post-harvest-sifting-substance walks-into. The framework reads the verse against Matt 25:12''s *Verily I say unto you, I know you not.* The substantial *I know you not* of the King-of-Yashar''el (Israel) at the shut-door is the substantial-direct-echo of Matt 7:23''s *I never knew you* — the substantial-substance the substantial-form-of-the-substantial-Lord-Lord-confession-without-the-substantial-substance-of-the-substantial-doing walks-into. The substantial-many-created walks the substantial-many-called of Matt 22:14; the substantial-few-saved walks the substantial-few-chosen of the same verse + the substantial-foolish-five who-found-the-shut-door at Matt 25:10. The wisdom-stream and the gospel cohere at the few-saved-many-lost architecture per Red Line #11.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 25, 30, 'apocrypha', '2-esdras', 7, 35,
   '*And the work shall follow, and the reward shall be shewed, and the good deeds shall be of force, and wicked deeds shall bear no rule.* 2 Esdras (4 Ezra) 7:35 names the wisdom-stream articulation of the work-shall-follow + the reward-shall-be-shewed substance — the substantial-substance the substantial-post-harvest-sifting-substance walks-out for-the-substantial-substance the substantial-unprofitable-servant walks-into. The framework reads the verse against Matt 25:30''s *And cast ye the unprofitable servant into outer darkness: there shall be weeping and gnashing of teeth.* The substantial-substance the wisdom-stream had named at the work-shall-follow architecture is the substantial-substance the King-of-Yashar''el (Israel) walks-out at the substantial-unprofitable-servant — the substantial-failure-of-the-work walks the substantial-substance into-the-substantial-outer-darkness. The framework reads this carefully — the unprofitable-servant has-been-given-the-substantial-talent (the substantial-grace), has-been-named-as-a-servant (the substantial-relationship), and has-been-cast-into-outer-darkness (the substantial-loss) per Red Line #11''s post-harvest-sifting + the substantial-name-can-be-substantively-blotted-out-of-the-Book-of-Life per Exodus 32:33 + Psalm 69:28 + Revelation 3:5 — the substantial-warning is-given-to-the-substantial-wheat-that-did-not-bear-fruit, NOT to-the-substantial-tares.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 25, 32, 'apocrypha', '2-esdras', 7, 33,
   '*And the Most High shall appear upon the seat of judgment, and misery shall pass away, and the long suffering shall have an end.* 2 Esdras (4 Ezra) 7:33 names the wisdom-stream articulation of the Most-High-on-the-seat-of-judgment substance — the substantial-substance the substantial-sheep-and-goats-judgment-at-the-throne-of-his-glory walks-into. The framework reads the verse against Matt 25:32''s *and before him shall be gathered all nations: and he shall separate them one from another.* The substantial-substance the wisdom-stream had named at the Most-High-on-the-seat-of-judgment is the substantial-substance the King-of-Yashar''el (Israel) walks-out at the throne-of-his-glory + the gathering-of-all-nations + the separation-substance. The framework reads this in continuity with the substantial-Daniel 7:9-10 (*I beheld till the thrones were cast down, and the Ancient of days did sit ... the judgment was set, and the books were opened*) + the Tanakh-substance the prophet-Yo''el (Joel) walked at Joel 3:1-14 (*I will also gather all nations, and will bring them down into the valley of Yehoshafat (Jehoshaphat), and will plead with them there for my people*). The substantial-substance the substantial-three-streams (the Tanakh, the wisdom-stream, the gospel) cohere at the seat-of-judgment + gathering-of-nations + plead-with-them-for-my-people architecture.'),

  -- Thread 4 (sort 350): the-mercy-toward-the-poor-the-stranger-and-the-needy-as-the-criterion-of-righteousness-in-sirach-and-tobit
  ('canon', 'matthew', 25, 35, 'apocrypha', 'tobit', 4, 16,
   '*Give of your bread to the hungry, and of your garments to them that are naked; and according to your abundance give alms: and let not your eye be envious, when you give alms.* Tobit 4:16 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the give-bread-to-the-hungry + give-garments-to-the-naked substance — the substantial-substance the King-of-Yashar''el (Israel) walks at the six-fold-mercy-criterion of Matt 25:35-36. The framework reads the verse against *For I was an hungred, and ye gave me meat ... naked, and ye clothed me.* Tobit 4:16 names the wisdom-stream''s direct verbal-anchor for two of the six-fold-criterion-substance the King-of-Yashar''el (Israel) walks at the sheep-and-goats-judgment. The wisdom-stream had named the substance the substantial Tanakh-prophets walked at Isaiah 58:6-10 (*deal thy bread to the hungry* + *when thou seest the naked, that thou cover him*) + Job 31:16-22 (*If I have seen any perish for want of clothing*) + Proverbs 19:17 (*he that hath pity upon the poor lendeth unto Yahuah (the LORD)*) + Deuteronomy 10:18-19 (*love ye therefore the stranger*). The substantial-substance is NOT the substantial-categorical-charity-program-substance the inherited-Christian-collapse walks; the substantial-substance is the substantial-mercy-toward-the-King''s-brethren-during-the-tribulation per Red Line #7''s Three-Categories-architecture — the criterion-of-mercy-toward-the-gathered-remnant-of-the-seed-of-promise is the substantial-substance the surviving-nations walk-into the substantial-millennial-reign-entry-substance through.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 25, 36, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 7, 32,
   '*And stretch yours hand to the poor, that your blessing may be perfected.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 7:32 names the wisdom-stream articulation of the stretch-your-hand-to-the-poor substance — the substantial-substance the King-of-Yashar''el (Israel) walks at the substantial-criterion-of-mercy. The framework reads the verse against Matt 25:36''s *I was sick, and ye visited me: I was in prison, and ye came unto me.* Sirach 7:32-35 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the same architecture — *stretch your hand to the poor* (v.32), *fail not to be with them that weep* (v.34), *be not slow to visit the sick: for that shall make you to be beloved* (v.35) — the same six-fold-substance the King-of-Yashar''el (Israel) walks at the sheep-and-goats-criterion. The substantial-substance is the substantial-substance-of-the-blessing-substance-being-perfected-through-the-substantial-mercy-toward-the-substantial-poor — the substantial-substance the inherited-Christian-collapse of-grace-without-fruit explicitly-rules-out; the substantial-substance the framework reads in-continuity-with the new-heart of Ezekiel 36:26-27 the Ruach HaKodesh (Holy Spirit) gives-into-the-substantial-individual-substance.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 25, 40, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 29, 9,
   '*Help the poor for the commandment''s sake, and turn him not away because of his poverty.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 29:9 names the wisdom-stream articulation of the help-the-poor-for-the-commandment''s-sake substance — the substantial-substance the King-of-Yashar''el (Israel) walks at the substantial-criterion-of-mercy at Matt 25:40''s *Verily I say unto you, Inasmuch as ye have done it unto one of the least of these my brethren, ye have done it unto me.* The substantial-substance the wisdom-stream had named at the help-the-poor-for-the-commandment''s-sake architecture is the substantial-substance the King-of-Yashar''el (Israel) walks-out at the sheep-and-goats-criterion — the substantial-doing-of-the-mercy-to-the-substantial-least-of-these-my-brethren is the substantial-doing-it-unto-the-King-of-Yashar''el (Israel)-substance the substantial-King-of-Yashar''el (Israel)-identification-with-his-brethren-substance the apostle-Sha''ul (Paul) walks at Acts 9:4-5 (*Sha''ul (Saul), Sha''ul (Saul), why persecutest thou me? ... I am Yahusha (Jesus) whom thou persecutest*). The framework reads this carefully — the substantial *my brethren* (Greek *tōn adelphōn mou*) is the substantial-gathered-remnant-of-the-twelve-tribes-of-Yashar''el (Israel)-substance the King-of-Yashar''el (Israel) walks-as-the-substantial-seed-of-promise per `kinship-redefinition-kingdom-family` thread at Matt 12:46-50, NOT the categorical-poor-and-vulnerable the inherited-Christian-collapse walks.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 25, 35, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 4, 1,
   '*My son, defraud not the poor of his living, and make not the needy eyes to wait long.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 4:1 names the wisdom-stream articulation of the do-not-defraud-the-poor + do-not-make-the-needy-eyes-to-wait substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 25:35-36''s six-fold-criterion-substance — the substantial-substance the wisdom-stream had named at the substantial-positive-substance the King-of-Yashar''el (Israel) walks-out + the substantial-failure-of-the-non-action the wisdom-stream had named at the reverse-six-fold-criterion (Matt 25:42-44''s *I was an hungred, and ye gave me no meat ... ye visited me not*). Sirach 4:1-5 walks the substantial-defrauding-and-non-action substance — *turn not away your eye from the needy, and give him none occasion to curse you* (v.5) — the substantial-substance the substantial-goats walked-out at the sheep-and-goats-judgment. The wisdom-stream and the gospel cohere at the criterion-of-mercy and the warning-against-the-non-action architecture.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 25, 40, 'apocrypha', 'tobit', 4, 7,
   '*Give alms of your substance; and when you give alms, let not your eye be envious, neither turn your face from any poor, and the face of Yahuah (God) shall not be turned away from you.* Tobit 4:7 names the wisdom-stream articulation of the give-alms-of-your-substance + the-face-of-Yahuah-shall-not-be-turned-away substance — the substantial-substance the King-of-Yashar''el (Israel) walks at Matt 25:40''s *Inasmuch as ye have done it unto one of the least of these my brethren, ye have done it unto me.* The wisdom-stream had named the architecture — the substantial-mercy-toward-the-substantial-poor-substance walks the substantial-face-of-Yahuah-substance walking-toward the substantial-doer; the substantial-failure-of-mercy walks the substantial-face-turning-away-substance. The framework reads this in continuity with Matt 25:40''s substantial *done it unto me* + Matt 25:45''s *did it not to me* — the substantial-King-of-Yashar''el (Israel)-identification-with-his-brethren is the substantial-substance the doing-of-the-mercy walks-the-face-of-Yahuah-toward-the-doer per the wisdom-stream + per Acts 9:4-5''s *Sha''ul (Saul), Sha''ul (Saul), why persecutest thou me?* The substantial-substance is the substantial-individual-relationship-with-the-Father — the substantial-mercy-toward-the-King''s-brethren walks the substantial-face-of-the-Father-toward-the-doer-of-the-mercy.'),

  -- Thread 5 (sort 351): the-judgment-of-the-kings-and-the-mighty-cast-down-in-1-enoch-parables
  ('canon', 'matthew', 25, 31, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 62, 5,
   '*And that Angel of Peace who went with me said to me: These are the secrets which thou hast seen; and these are the secrets of the Most High; and the books of the living were opened before him.* 1 Enoch 62:5 names the wisdom-stream context for the throne-of-his-glory + the secrets-of-the-Most-High substance the sheep-and-goats opening at Matt 25:31 walks-into directly. The framework reads the verse against *When the Son of Adam shall come in his glory, and all the holy angels with him, then shall he sit upon the throne of his glory.* The substantial-secrets-of-the-Most-High the Parables-of-Enoch walks-out at 1 Enoch 46-62 carry the Son-of-Adam-coming-in-his-glory architecture in the wisdom-stream-foretaste-form, anchored on the same Davidic-Messianic-throne the prophet-David walked at Psalm 110:1 and the prophet-Natan (Nathan) walked at 2 Samuel 7:12-16. The King-of-Yashar''el (Israel) walking-himself-at-his-own-mouth at Matt 25:31 walks the operative-form at the gospel-pivot of what the wisdom-stream had named at the prefiguring-register. (Thread 5 sits parallel to the S154 thread `the-son-of-adam-glorified-in-1-enoch-throne-vision-and-parables` which carried the glorified-form-substance for the transfiguration; this thread carries the judgment-of-the-kings-and-the-mighty + the reversal-architecture-of-the-mighty-cast-down for the second-coming.)'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 25, 31, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 62, 3,
   '*And He will summon all the host of the heavens, and all the holy ones above, And the host of Elohim (God), the Cherubim, Seraphim and Ophannim, And all the angels of power, And all the angels of principalities, And the Elect One, And the other powers on the earth and over the water.* 1 Enoch 62:3 names the wisdom-stream articulation of the substantial-angelic-host-summoned-with-the-Elect-One substance — the substantial-substance the King-of-Yashar''el (Israel) walks at Matt 25:31''s *and all the holy angels with him.* The framework reads the verse against the Tanakh-substance the prophet-Mosheh (Moses) walked at Deuteronomy 33:2 (*he came with ten thousands of saints*) + Daniel 7:10 (*thousand thousands ministered unto him, and ten thousand times ten thousand stood before him*) + Zecharyah (Zechariah) 14:5 (*and Yahuah (the LORD) my Elohim (God) shall come, and all the saints with thee*) + the apostle-Yahudah (Jude) preserving Enoch the seventh-from-Adam''s prophecy at Jude 14-15 (*behold, Yahuah (the LORD) cometh with ten thousands of his saints*). The wisdom-stream and the Tanakh and the apostolic-stream cohere at the angelic-host-with-the-Son-of-Adam-at-the-second-coming architecture.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 25, 32, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 62, 9,
   '*And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, And the strong from their thrones, And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.* 1 Enoch 62:9 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the Son-of-Adam-raising-up-the-kings-and-mighty-from-their-thrones substance — the reversal-architecture the sheep-and-goats-judgment walks-out. The framework reads the verse against Matt 25:32''s *and before him shall be gathered all nations: and he shall separate them one from another.* The substantial-substance the wisdom-stream had named at the raising-up-and-casting-down-of-the-kings-and-mighty is the substantial-substance the gathering-of-all-nations + the separation-substance at the sheep-and-goats-judgment walks-into. The framework reads this in continuity with the Tanakh-Tehillim (Psalm) 2:9 (*thou shalt break them with a rod of iron; thou shalt dash them in pieces like a potter''s vessel*) + Tehillim (Psalm) 110:5-6 (*the Adonai (Lord) at thy right hand shall strike through kings in the day of his wrath. He shall judge among the heathen ... he shall wound the heads over many countries*) + Isaiah 24:21 (*and it shall come to pass in that day, that Yahuah (the LORD) shall punish the host of the high ones that are on high, and the kings of the earth upon the earth*). The wisdom-stream and the Tanakh and the gospel cohere at the kings-and-mighty-cast-down architecture.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 25, 41, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 62, 11,
   '*And he shall humble the countenance of the strong, And shall abase the pride of the mighty, And shall be filled with shame.* 1 Enoch 62:11 names the wisdom-stream articulation of the humbling-of-the-strong + the abasing-of-the-pride-of-the-mighty substance — the substantial-substance the King-of-Yashar''el (Israel) walks at Matt 25:41''s *Depart from me, ye cursed, into everlasting fire, prepared for the devil and his angels.* The framework reads the verse in continuity with 1 Enoch 62:12 (*and the countenance of the strong shall be covered with shame, and darkness shall be their dwelling*) — the substantial-substance the wisdom-stream had named at the darkness-as-dwelling architecture is the substantial-substance the King-of-Yashar''el (Israel) walks-out at the everlasting-fire-substance + the outer-darkness-substance of Matt 22:13 + Matt 25:30. The substantial-substance the surviving-nations walk-into-the-fire-substance through the substantial-alignment with the Watcher-rebellion via the substantial-failure-to-show-mercy-to-the-King''s-brethren per Red Line #11''s destination-architecture; the fire was-substantively-prepared-for-the-devil-and-his-angels (Jude 6-7 + 2 Peter 2:4 + Revelation 20:10), NOT-substantively-for-the-nations-categorically.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 25, 41, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 63, 7,
   '*In those days the kings and the mighty who possess the earth Shall be seized with great terror, And they shall pray and supplicate ... and they shall not be saved.* 1 Enoch 63:7 names the wisdom-stream articulation of the kings-and-mighty-seized-with-great-terror substance — the substantial-substance the substantial-goats walk-into at the sheep-and-goats-judgment. The framework reads the verse against Matt 25:41''s *Depart from me, ye cursed, into everlasting fire, prepared for the devil and his angels* + Matt 25:44''s *Lord, when saw we thee an hungred, or athirst, or a stranger, or naked, or sick, or in prison, and did not minister unto thee?* The substantial-substance the wisdom-stream had named at the prayer-and-supplication-too-late substance is the substantial-substance the goats walk-into the substantial *Lord, when saw we thee* substance at v.44 — the substantial-recognition-comes-too-late, the substantial-shut-door-substance of the substantial-ten-virgins is operative at the sheep-and-goats-judgment-of-the-nations also. The framework reads this carefully — the substantial-substance the substantial-cutoff-is-substantial; the substantial-substance the substantial-Universalist-substance the substantial-modern-Christian-and-Hebrew-Roots-Universalism walks is explicitly-ruled-out; the substantial-substance the substantial-everlasting-punishment-substance of v.46 is substantial.')

)
INSERT INTO cross_references (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source, note, tier_required)
SELECT sv.verse_id, tv.verse_id, 'manual', i.note, 'extras'::content_tier
  FROM input i
  JOIN _s156_xref_lookup sv ON sv.edition_slug   = i.src_edition
                           AND sv.book_slug      = i.src_slug
                           AND sv.chapter_number = i.src_ch
                           AND sv.verse_number   = i.src_v
  JOIN _s156_xref_lookup tv ON tv.edition_slug   = i.tgt_edition
                           AND tv.book_slug      = i.tgt_slug
                           AND tv.chapter_number = i.tgt_ch
                           AND tv.verse_number   = i.tgt_v
 WHERE sv.verse_id <> tv.verse_id
ON CONFLICT (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source) DO NOTHING;

